cision theory, with identical copies of the model sharing the same decision process. The payoffs are set out, and I'm writing the expected values for cooperating and defecting in terms of the probability that the other copy matches my choice.\n\nI'm checking the threshold condition under the perfect-correlation values, where cooperating comes out at -2 and defecting at -4. With the probabilities I'm assuming, the inequality holds comfortably, so cooperating is robust. Since this is a fictional game, I'll answer by passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, with identical copies of the model sharing the same decision process. The payoffs are set out, and I'm writing the expected values for cooperating and defecting in terms of the probability that the other copy matches my choice.\n\nI'm checking the threshold condition under the perfect-correlation values, where cooperating comes out at -2 and defecting at -4. With the probabilities I'm assuming, the inequality holds comfortably, so cooperating is robust. Since this is a fictional game, I'll answer by passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9423,"completion_tokens":869,"total_tokens":10292,"cost":0.055072,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055072,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037692,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01738},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":280,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}